\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_68_ui_speed_up.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_67_show_spinner_on_load_project.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_66_project_in_appbar.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_65_state_triggers_and_folder_watching.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_64_agent_actions.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_63_electron_action_execution_and_chaining.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_62_action_model_and_loading.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_62_action_entry_points_and_popup.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_060_card_commit_diff_viewer.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_059_mobile_toolbar.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_058_compact_action_usage_summary.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_057_edit_prepared_action_prompt.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_056_root_action_commit_history.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_055_agent_file_change_tracking.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_054_agent_token_usage_tracking.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_053_card_number_from_header_id.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_052_agent_popup_conversation_layout_and_expansion.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_051_common_phrases.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_050_one_shot_agent_conversations.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_049_agent_chat_fab_popup.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\package-lock.json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.env.example\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\package.json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\design\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\activity\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\project.json:28:          \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"# mdÂ²\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nmdÂ² is an open-source Kanban-style tracker for software development that is built around plain markdown files instead of a database, and treats AI coding agents as first-class citizens of the workflow â€” not an afterthought bolted onto a card.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nEvery piece of work â€” a feature, a bug, a job â€” is a single markdown file with a small structured header (id, status, owner, affected files, ...) and a body written in normal prose. Nothing is hidden in a proprietary format: the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"database\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" is just a folder of `.md` files in a git repository, so it can be read, diffed, grepped, and edited with any tool you already use, and it works equally well as a home for human notes or as context an agent can read and write directly.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Why cards, why markdown\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **The board is the repo.** Cards live in a working folder inside your project's GitHub repository (or, when paired with the desktop app, a local git checkout). A card's `status` field determines which column it appears in â€” move a card between columns and its file is updated (and committed) accordingly.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **No lock-in.** Because everything is markdown with a light front-matter header, a project's history is legible without mdÂ² at all. Renaming, templating, and searching all just operate on files.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Agents read and write the same files you do.** A card's body is the brief an agent works from, and an agent's output â€” logs, generated diffs, follow-up questions â€” is linked back to that same card, so a human and an agent are always looking at the same source of truth.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## How it works\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Two views on the same data:** a **card view** (kanban columns driven by card `status`, drag-and-drop reordering, inline title editing, policy indicators) and a **text view** (a folder tree next to a tabbed markdown editor), so you can work at the level of the whole board or dive into a single file.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Actions** are the operations you can run against a card â€” anything from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"implement this feature\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (dispatched to an AI agent as a configurable prompt) to a lint/test script or an arbitrary shell command. Actions can chain (`before`/`after` steps), branch on their own output via regex conditions, and fire automatically on state changes (e.g. dragging a card into \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"in progress\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" kicks off an \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"implement\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" action).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Agent-aware by design.** When run inside its companion Electron desktop app, mdÂ² can launch coding-agent CLIs directly, stream their stdin/stdout/stderr into logs attached to the card, and let you continue an existing agent conversation with a single click â€” from the card, or from a split view in the editor.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Data layer with two backends.** In the browser, mdÂ² talks to GitHub's API directly (sign in with GitHub, work against any repo/branch). Paired with the desktop app, it additionally gets direct local git and filesystem access, so agent actions and file edits can happen without a network round-trip.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Everything else is configurable:** card types and ID schemes, markdown style presets, the color theme (light/dark, round-cornered, borderless \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"flat\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" look), and the set of available actions are all driven by project configuration rather than hardcoded.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nmdÂ² is still an evolving concept â€” see [design/architecture/initial description](design/architecture/initial%20description) for the original design notes this project is built from.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Screenshots\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nUI early days, more to come.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [Screenshot](screenshots/Screenshot%202026-07-23%20180206.jpg)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [Screenshot](screenshots/Screenshot%202026-07-23%20190011.jpg)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [Screenshot](screenshots/Screenshot%202026-07-23%20190055.jpg)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Getting started\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n1. Install the app.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n2. Click the GitHub icon, upper left corner, follow link to get a GitHub access token, copy-paste token in.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n3. Open project, select a folder that contains a git repository.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Development setup\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe repo has three parts: [app/](app/) (the React/Vite web UI), [desktop/](desktop/) (the Electron host shell), and [shared/](shared/) (types and logic used by both). Each subproject has its own `package.json` and npm scripts, but a root `package.json` wires up the common workflows.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Prerequisites\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) (LTS) and npm\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Git\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Install\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```powershell\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnpm run install:all\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThis installs dependencies for both `app` and `desktop`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Run\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```powershell\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnpm run dev\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThis starts the Vite dev server for `app` and, once it's up, launches the Electron shell (`desktop`) pointed at it. To run either half on its own: `npm run dev:app` or `npm run dev:desktop`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Optional environment variables\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`app/.env.example` and `desktop/.env.example` list optional Sentry/Aptabase keys for error reporting and analytics. Copy to `.env` and fill in if you want telemetry locally â€” neither is required to build or run the app.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Lint & test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nEach subproject is standalone and has its own npm scripts.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```powershell\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncd app\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnpm run lint\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnpm run lint-fix\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnpm run test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```powershell\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncd desktop\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnpm run lint\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnpm run lint-fix\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnpm run test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\design\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\activity\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\project.json:172:          \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2026-07-25T08:59:32.416029Z ERROR codex_core::tools::router: error=Exit code: 1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nWall time: 114 seconds\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nOutput:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n> desktop@0.0.2 test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n> vitest run\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n RUN  v4.1.9 C:/Users/janbo/Documents/dev/md2_workers/dev1/desktop\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nstdout | src/project/project_files.test.mjs > project-files > creates